300 (0.73x), which suggests there's something inefficient happening at larger problem sizes that I need to investigate. .42x (good scaling)\n- WHIR: 218ms → 128ms = 1.70x\n- Stacked Reduction: 78ms → 75ms = 1.04x (no scaling!)\n\nSo the issue is:\n1. LogUp GKR scales 1.85x (should be >2x given 2x reduction in interactions)\n2. Round 0 doesn't scale at all (178→181ms)\n3. MLE Rounds actually gets WORSE with more APCs (118→161ms)\n4. Stacked Reduction doesn't scale (78→75ms)\n5. Trace Commit scales well (2.42x)\n6. WHIR scales somewhat (1.70x)\n\nThe overall STARK excl trace scales 1791/1129 = 1.59x.\n\nThe main bottlenecks are LogUp GKR at 383ms, MLE Rounds which regressed to 161ms, Round 0 stuck at 181ms, and WHIR at 128ms. Round 0 is interesting though—it's been massively optimized from 662ms down to 181ms with the multi-stream approach, but now it's hitting a floor that doesn't improve with more APCs, suggesting the optimization has saturated and we're limited by something else in the pipeline.\n\nMLE Rounds is the real problem—it's taking longer with more APCs because there are way more traces to process (623 vs 99), and the per-trace overhead adds up even though each individual trace is smaller.\n\nI should profile with nsight to see what's actually happening on the GPU for both APC 0 and APC 300, and compare against the baseline to understand where the remaining bottlenecks are.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2678,"cache_read_input_tokens":73511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2678},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"e539651e-581d-4c4f-b74a-1ae282e59ffb"}
