{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a17027b91f10593f0","tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7wTUwCB4kx1fVvip9Z9LN","description":"Review optimization plan","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are a plan reviewer for a GPU prover optimization project. Review the following plan following the review guideline.\n\nRead these files:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0200-cache-monomial-products-for-dead-traces/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nAdditionally, you should verify the plan against the actual codebase:\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` to verify the code paths described in the plan match reality\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/monomial.rs` to understand what the monomial kernels actually compute\n- Verify the `compute_batch_s_poly` function handles late traces as described\n- Check how `lambda_combinations` and `logup_combinations` are stored and updated\n\nThe key questions to answer:\n1. Is the claim correct that matrix values are constant for height-1 traces across MLE rounds?\n2. Is the caching mechanism correctly designed (what exactly to cache, when to cache it)?\n3. Are the estimated savings realistic given the nsight profiling data?\n4. Are there hidden interface mismatches or correctness issues?\n\nReturn your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n","uuid":"c805c390-f9d4-4e4a-bc7e-99f44b7fac86","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a plan reviewer for a GPU prover optimization project. Review the following plan following the review guideline.\n\nRead these files:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0200-cache-monomial-products-for-dead-traces/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nAdditionally, you should verify the plan against the actual codebase:\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` to verify the code paths described in the plan match reality\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/monomial.rs` to understand what the monomial kernels actually compute\n- Verify the `compute_batch_s_poly` function handles late traces as described\n- Check how `lambda_combinations` and `logup_combinations` are stored and updated\n\nThe key questions to answer:\n1. Is the claim correct that matrix values are constant for height-1 traces across MLE rounds?\n2. Is the caching mechanism correctly designed (what exactly to cache, when to cache it)?\n3. Are the estimated savings realistic given the nsight profiling data?\n4. Are there hidden interface mismatches or correctness issues?\n\nReturn your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7wTUwCB4kx1fVvip9Z9LN","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"5e7addaf-b0cf-491d-9972-1beda77ebda3","timestamp":"2026-04-16T00:01:34.777Z"}
