{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013xa5NsDcQ4ustBuKDKADyT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0200-cache-monomial-products-for-dead-traces\n2\t\n3\tIn MLE sumcheck rounds, traces that have been fully folded to height 1 (\"late_eval\" / dead traces) still have GPU monomial evaluation kernels launched every round (zerocheck_monomial_kernel: 17ms, zerocheck_monomial_par_y_kernel: 18ms, logup_monomial_kernel: 6ms = ~41ms total at APC 300). For these traces, the matrix values are constant across rounds — only the lambda_comb weights change. By caching the per-monomial products once when a trace first becomes height-1 and computing the weighted sum on CPU each subsequent round, we eliminate the GPU kernel launches and D2H syncs, saving ~30-35ms at APC 300 with minimal impact at APC 0 where fewer traces are height-1.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01J7wTUwCB4kx1fVvip9Z9LN","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"b2ff96a0-682e-4420-b096-abe76ca27bde","timestamp":"2026-04-16T00:03:52.392Z"}
