{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a5af4d771050836bf","tool_use_id":"toolu_0192Qvd465i9XpeWnmukTiDV","description":"Review revised optimization plan","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are a plan reviewer for a GPU prover optimization project. Review the following plan following the review guideline.\n\nRead these files:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0200-batch-fold-ple-descriptor-array/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nAdditionally, verify the plan against the actual codebase:\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` lines 688-788 to verify the per-trace loop exists as described\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` to verify the kernel signature and launch parameters match the plan\n- Check how `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel` relates to `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` (are they the same kernel under different names?)\n- Verify the kernel's grid/block dimensions match what the plan says\n- Check if there are existing descriptor-array patterns in the codebase that this follows\n\nKey questions to answer:\n1. Is the per-trace sequential kernel launch pattern accurately described?\n2. Will the batched kernel actually enable concurrent SM utilization (or are there synchronization barriers)?\n3. Is the expected savings (8-12ms) plausible given the nsight data (9.5ms total, 797 instances)?\n4. Are the BlockCtx/descriptor struct designs correct and complete?\n\nReturn your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n","uuid":"dc02adfd-0f5e-4c22-9ecd-c06813632fa0","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a plan reviewer for a GPU prover optimization project. Review the following plan following the review guideline.\n\nRead these files:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0200-batch-fold-ple-descriptor-array/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nAdditionally, verify the plan against the actual codebase:\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs` lines 688-788 to verify the per-trace loop exists as described\n- Check `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu` to verify the kernel signature and launch parameters match the plan\n- Check how `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel` relates to `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` (are they the same kernel under different names?)\n- Verify the kernel's grid/block dimensions match what the plan says\n- Check if there are existing descriptor-array patterns in the codebase that this follows\n\nKey questions to answer:\n1. Is the per-trace sequential kernel launch pattern accurately described?\n2. Will the batched kernel actually enable concurrent SM utilization (or are there synchronization barriers)?\n3. Is the expected savings (8-12ms) plausible given the nsight data (9.5ms total, 797 instances)?\n4. Are the BlockCtx/descriptor struct designs correct and complete?\n\nReturn your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0192Qvd465i9XpeWnmukTiDV","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"e25e9834-9bbf-462c-8688-850c7a47c5ca","timestamp":"2026-04-16T00:12:57.937Z"}
