{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QZBqKXBA1WR47ViARYYKJG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0200-batch-fold-ple-descriptor-array\n2\t\n3\tThe Stacked Reduction's `fold_ple_evals` function launches one `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` GPU kernel per unstacked trace in a sequential loop (lines 714-742 of `stacked_reduction.rs`). At APC 300, this creates ~600-800 individual kernel launches per proof across 2 segments. Each launch averages 12μs but serializes on the GPU stream, preventing concurrent SM utilization across traces. Replacing the per-trace loop with a single descriptor-array batched kernel launch enables concurrent processing of all traces on different SMs, converting the current sum-of-kernel-times (~9.5ms) into a max-of-kernel-times (~2ms) while also eliminating ~790 kernel launch overhead cycles (~4ms). Expected savings: ~10ms at APC 300.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0192Qvd465i9XpeWnmukTiDV","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"a0cd3445-4625-4ecc-a7a3-6d5a755616fd","timestamp":"2026-04-16T00:13:01.700Z"}
