{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01S3rXpmE11jLy9UG7HbCDLR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01St44Lc44zQa6UMtjqLzxw8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0200-batch-fold-ple-descriptor-array/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Batch fold_ple_from_evals Kernel Launches via Descriptor Array\n\n## Goal\n\nReplace the per-trace sequential `fold_ple_from_evals` GPU kernel launches in `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594) with a single batched descriptor-array kernel. nsight shows `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>`: 797 instances, 9.5ms total at APC 300. The per-trace loop launches one kernel per matrix per trace, serializing on the GPU stream. A batched launch enables concurrent block scheduling across traces.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Entry: `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594)\n\nCalled once per segment at line 619, inside the Round 0 tracing span (after `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, before MLE rounds begin).\n\nThe function iterates all traces and launches `fold_ple_from_evals` per matrix:\n\n```rust\nself.mat_evals_per_trace = ctx.per_trace.iter().map(|(air_idx, air_ctx)| {\n    let mut results: Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>> = Vec::new();\n    // Preprocessed (if exists): fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 kernel launches\n    if let Some(committed) = &air_pk.preprocessed_data {\n        results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n    }\n    // Cached mains: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches each\n    for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains { ... }\n    // Common main: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches\n    results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n    Ok(results)\n}).collect()?;\n```\n\n### `fold_ple_evals_rotate` (fold_ple.rs:16-55)\n\nCalls `fold_ple_evals_gpu` once (rotate=false), and if `need_rot`, once more (rotate=true). Each call allocates a separate output buffer, then launches the kernel.\n\n### `fold_ple_evals_gpu` → `fold_ple_from_evals` (fold_ple.rs:67-102)\n\nFFI call to `_fold_ple_from_evals` in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`. Kernel: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<ROTATE>`.\n\nGrid: `(ceil(num_x / chunks_per_block), width)`, block: `max(256, skip_domain)`.\n\nPer-thread: barycentric interpolation of `min(height, skip_domain)` source values into one output EF value. When `ROTATE=true`, source values are shifted by one position (modular rotation).\n\n### Parameters per launch\n\n- `src`: matrix data pointer (`*const F`)\n- `dst`: output pointer (`*mut EF`)\n- `omega_skip_pows`: shared across all traces\n- `inv_lagrange_denoms`: shared across all traces\n- `height`, `width`, `l_skip`, `num_x`: per-trace dimensions\n- `rotate`: bool (template parameter)\n\n### Why it's slow at APC 300\n\n797 kernel launches at avg 12μs each = 9.5ms GPU time. Two costs:\n1. **Kernel launch overhead**: ~5μs × 797 = ~4ms of CUDA driver overhead.\n2. **Serial SM utilization**: Small traces (low width × low num_x) produce few blocks, leaving most of the 128 SMs idle while each small kernel runs to completion.\n\nAt APC 0: ~200 traces × ~1.3 matrices = ~260 launches across 5 segments. Savings proportionally smaller.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Define descriptor struct (CUDA side)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n\n```c\nstruct FoldPleDesc {\n    const Fp *src;       // source matrix data pointer\n    FpExt *dst;          // output buffer pointer (non-overlapping per trace)\n    uint32_t height;     // source matrix height\n    uint32_t width;      // source matrix width\n    uint32_t num_x;      // = max(height, skip_domain) / skip_domain\n};\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add batched kernel using prefix-sum block mapping\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n\nFollow the existing `batched_nondegen_mle_round_kernel` pattern: upload a prefix-sum array of cumulative block counts, and each CUDA block binary-searches to find its descriptor index.\n\n```c\ntemplate <bool ROTATE>\n__global__ void batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel(\n    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n    const uint32_t *prefix_blocks,  // prefix_blocks[i] = sum of blocks for descs 0..i-1\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    uint32_t skip_domain\n) {\n    // Binary search to find which descriptor this block belongs to\n    uint32_t desc_idx = upper_bound(prefix_blocks, num_descs, blockIdx.x) - 1;\n    auto desc = descs[desc_idx];\n    uint32_t local_block = blockIdx.x - prefix_blocks[desc_idx];\n\n    // Decompose local_block into (row_chunk_idx, col_idx) using desc.width\n    uint32_t chunks_per_block = blockDim.x / skip_domain;\n    uint32_t blocks_per_col = (desc.num_x + chunks_per_block - 1) / chunks_per_block;\n    uint32_t col_idx = local_block / blocks_per_col;\n    uint32_t row_block = local_block % blocks_per_col;\n\n    // Same body as existing fold_ple_from_evals_kernel but reading src/dst/dims from desc\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Step 3: Add C launcher and FFI bindings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n\n```c\nextern \"C\" int _batched_fold_ple_from_evals(\n    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n    const uint32_t *prefix_blocks,\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    uint32_t total_blocks,\n    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    uint32_t l_skip,\n    bool rotate\n);\n```\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nAdd `#[repr(C)]` struct `FoldPleDesc`, extern \"C\" declaration, and safe Rust wrapper. The wrapper signature:\n\n```rust\npub fn batched_fold_ple_from_evals(\n    d_descs: &DeviceBuffer<FoldPleDesc>,\n    d_prefix_blocks: &DeviceBuffer<u32>,\n    num_descs: u32,\n    total_blocks: u32,\n    omega_skip_pows: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    inv_lagrange_denoms: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    l_skip: u32,\n    rotate: bool,\n) -> Result<(), KernelError>;\n```\n\n### Step 4: Add batched dispatch in fold_ple_evals\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fold_ple.rs`\n\nAdd a new public function:\n\n```rust\npub fn batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate(\n    l_skip: usize,\n    d_omega_skip_pows: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    traces: &[(/*src*/ &DeviceMatrix<F>, /*need_rot*/ bool)],\n    d_inv_lagrange_denoms: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n) -> Result<Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>>, FoldPleError>\n```\n\nThis function:\n1. Pre-allocates output buffers for all traces (same as existing: per-trace `DeviceBuffer::with_capacity`).\n2. Builds descriptor arrays: one `FoldPleDesc` per trace for rotate=false, another for rotate=true (only traces with `need_rot`).\n3. Computes prefix block sums: for each descriptor, `blocks_i = ceil(num_x / chunks_per_block) * width`.\n4. Uploads descriptors + prefix sums to device.\n5. Two kernel launches: one for rotate=false (all traces), one for rotate=true (subset with need_rot).\n6. Returns `Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>>` matching the existing per-trace output format.\n\n### Step 5: Wire into fold_ple_evals\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, function `fold_ple_evals` (lines 1490-1538)\n\nReplace the per-trace iterator with:\n1. Collect all (trace_ref, need_rot) pairs from the per_trace iteration.\n2. Call `batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate(...)` with the collected pairs.\n3. Distribute the returned `Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>>` back into the per-trace `mat_evals_per_trace` structure.\n\n**Fallback**: If `traces.len() < 20`, use the existing per-trace path to avoid descriptor overhead for small workloads (APC 0 with ~20 AIRs per segment).\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Output equivalence**: Each trace's folded `DeviceMatrix<EF>` must match the per-trace kernel output bit-for-bit. The batched kernel performs identical computation per block.\n\n2. **Destination non-overlap**: Each descriptor's `dst` points to a separately allocated `DeviceBuffer`. No aliasing.\n\n3. **omega_skip_pows and inv_lagrange_denoms**: Shared across all traces. Passed as kernel parameters.\n\n4. **Block size**: Same as existing: `max(256, skip_domain)`. Shared memory allocation unchanged.\n\n5. **Per-trace output allocation preserved**: Each trace still gets its own `DeviceBuffer<EF>` and `DeviceMatrix`. The batched kernel writes to these individual buffers via per-descriptor `dst` pointers. The downstream code (`mat_evals_per_trace`) continues to work with the same per-trace matrix types.\n\n6. **Height=0 or width=0 traces**: Filtered out during descriptor building (matching the check at fold_ple.rs:78-80).\n\n7. **save_memory accounting**: The `mem_limit` subtraction for common_main traces (line 1533) still applies to the same folded buffers. The batched dispatch preserves the per-trace buffer sizes.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run benchmarks for APC {0, 100, 300}.\n2. Primary metric: Round 0 at APC 300 — expect ~6-8ms reduction (181ms → 173-175ms) from faster fold_ple_evals.\n3. STARK excl trace at APC 300 — expect same ~6-8ms reduction (1129ms → 1121-1123ms).\n4. APC 0: expect no regression (fallback path, < 20 traces per segment).\n5. nsight: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>` instances should drop from ~797 to ~2-4 (one batched launch per segment × 1-2 rotate variants).\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 < 3ms\n- APC 0 regression > 5ms on STARK excl trace\n- Correctness failure at any APC config\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1427,"cache_read_input_tokens":236087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1427},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"3b45fc90-36e6-458a-b450-15085d607d8a"}
