re at any APC config\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":201,"newStart":1,"newLines":207,"lines":["-# Plan: Batch fold_ple Kernel Launches via Descriptor Array","+# Plan: Batch fold_ple_from_evals Kernel Launches via Descriptor Array"," "," ## Goal"," ","-Replace the per-trace sequential loop of `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` GPU kernel launches in `fold_ple_evals` (stacked_reduction.rs:714-742) with a single batched descriptor-array kernel launch. At APC 300 with ~600-800 traces across 2 segments, this eliminates ~790 individual kernel launches and enables concurrent SM utilization across traces.","+Replace the per-trace sequential `fold_ple_from_evals` GPU kernel launches in `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594) with a single batched descriptor-array kernel. nsight shows `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>`: 797 instances, 9.5ms total at APC 300. The per-trace loop launches one kernel per matrix per trace, serializing on the GPU stream. A batched launch enables concurrent block scheduling across traces."," "," ## Current Code Path"," ","-### Rust side: `StackedReductionGpu::fold_ple_evals` (`stacked_reduction.rs:688-788`)","+### Entry: `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594)"," ","-After Round 0, this function folds PLE evaluations for each unstacked trace:","+Called once per segment at line 619, inside the Round 0 tracing span (after `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, before MLE rounds begin)."," ","+The function iterates all traces and launches `fold_ple_from_evals` per matrix:","+"," ```rust","-for stacked in &self.stacked_per_commit {           // ~2-3 commit groups","-    let folded_evals = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(num_x * stacked_width);","-    folded_evals.fill_zero()?;","-    let mut dst_offset = 0;","-    for trace in &stacked.traces {                   // ~300 traces at APC 300","-        stacked_reduction_fold_ple(                  // <-- One kernel launch per trace","-            trace.buffer().as_ptr(), dst, ...,","-            trace.height(), trace.width(), l_skip,","-        )?;","-        dst_offset += new_height * trace.width();","+self.mat_evals_per_trace = ctx.per_trace.iter().map(|(air_idx, air_ctx)| {","+    let mut results: Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>> = Vec::new();","+    // Preprocessed (if exists): fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 kernel launches","+    if let Some(committed) = &air_pk.preprocessed_data {","+        results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);","     }","-    self.q_evals.push(folded_evals);","-}","+    // Cached mains: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches each","+    for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains { ... }","+    // Common main: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches","+    results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);","+    Ok(results)","+}).collect()?;"," ```"," ","-Each `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` call launches `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` with grid `(ceil(new_height / chunks_per_block), trace_width)` and block `(max(256, skip_domain))`.","+### `fold_ple_evals_rotate` (fold_ple.rs:16-55)"," ","-### CUDA kernel: `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` (`stacked_reduction.cu:175-229`)","+Calls `fold_ple_evals_gpu` once (rotate=false), and if `need_rot`, once more (rotate=true). Each call allocates a separate output `DeviceBuffer`, then launches the kernel."," ","-Grid: 2D — `blockIdx.x` selects row chunk, `blockIdx.y` selects column.","-Per-thread: barycentric interpolation of `skip_domain` source values into one output FpExt value.","+### `fold_ple_evals_gpu` → `fold_ple_from_evals` (fold_ple.rs:67-102)"," ","-Parameters per trace: `src` (source trace pointer), `dst` (output pointer within folded_evals buffer), `trace_height`, `new_height`, `skip_domain`.","+FFI call to `_fold_ple_from_evals` in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`. Kernel: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<ROTATE>`."," ","-### Why it's slow","+Grid: `(ceil(num_x / chunks_per_block), width)`, block: `max(256, skip_domain)`."," ","-nsight profiling shows `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>` (same kernel, different instantiation): **797 instances, 9.5ms total, avg 12μs per instance**.","+Per-thread: barycentric interpolation of `min(height, skip_domain)` source values into one output EF value. When `ROTATE=true`, source values are shifted by one position (modular rotation)."," ","-Two costs:","-1. **Kernel launch overhead**: ~5μs × 797 = ~4ms. Each launch goes through the CUDA driver.","-2. **Sequential SM utilization**: Each per-trace kernel runs alone on the GPU. Small traces (low width × low height) use few blocks, leaving most of the 128 SMs idle. The next trace's kernel only starts after the previous completes.","+### Parameters per launch"," ","-With a batched kernel, all traces' blocks launch simultaneously. The GPU scheduler distributes them across SMs concurrently, converting sum-of-times into max-of-times.","+- `src`: matrix data pointer (`*const F`)","+- `dst`: output pointer (`*mut EF`)","+- `omega_skip_pows`: shared across all traces","+- `inv_lagrange_denoms`: shared across all traces","+- `height`, `width`, `l_skip`, `num_x`: per-trace dimensions","+- `rotate`: bool (template parameter)"," ","-## Changes","+### Why it's slow at APC 300"," ","-### Step 1: Define descriptor struct","+797 kernel launches at avg 12μs each = 9.5ms GPU time. Two costs:","+1. **Kernel launch overhead**: ~5μs × 797 = ~4ms of CUDA driver overhead.","+2. **Serial SM utilization**: Small traces (low width × low num_x) produce few blocks, leaving most of the 128 SMs idle while each small kernel runs to completion."," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`","+At APC 0: ~99 AIRs × ~1.3 matrices = ~130 launches across 5 segments, ~26 per segment. Savings proportionally smaller."," ","-Add a `FoldPleDesc` descriptor:","+## Changes"," ","-```c","-struct FoldPleDesc {","-    const Fp *src;          // source trace pointer","-    FpExt *dst;             // destination within folded_evals buffer","-    uint32_t trace_height;","-    uint32_t new_height;","-    uint32_t trace_width;","-};","-```","+### Step 1: Define descriptor struct (CUDA side)"," ","-### Step 2: Add BlockCtx mapping struct","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`","-","-Add a `FoldPleBlockCtx` that maps each CUDA block to a (descriptor_index, local_block_x, column_idx):","-"," ```c","-struct FoldPleBlockCtx {","-    uint32_t desc_idx;      // index into FoldPleDesc array","-    uint32_t local_block_x; // row chunk index within this trace","-    uint32_t col_idx;       // column index within this trace","+struct FoldPleDesc {","+    const Fp *src;       // source matrix data pointer","+    FpExt *dst;          // output buffer pointer (non-overlapping per trace)","+    uint32_t height;     // source matrix height","+    uint32_t width;      // source matrix width","+    uint32_t num_x;      // = max(height, skip_domain) / skip_domain"," };"," ```"," ","-### Step 3: Implement batched kernel","+### Step 2: Add batched kernel using prefix-sum block mapping"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`"," ","-Add `batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel`:","+Follow the existing `batched_nondegen_mle_round_kernel` pattern (in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/mle.cu`): upload a prefix-sum array of cumulative block counts, and each CUDA block binary-searches to find its descriptor index."," "," ```c","-__global__ void batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel(","-    const FoldPleBlockCtx *block_ctx,","+template <bool ROTATE>","+__global__ void batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel(","     const FoldPleDesc *descs,","+    const uint32_t *prefix_blocks,  // prefix_blocks[i] = sum of blocks for descs 0..i-1","+    uint32_t num_descs,","     const Fp *omega_skip_pows,","     const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,","     uint32_t skip_domain"," ) {","-    auto ctx = block_ctx[blockIdx.x];","-    auto desc = descs[ctx.desc_idx];","-    ","-    uint32_t col_idx = ctx.col_idx;","+    // Binary search to find which descriptor this block belongs to","+    uint32_t desc_idx = upper_bound(prefix_blocks, num_descs, blockIdx.x) - 1;","+    auto desc = descs[desc_idx];","+    uint32_t local_block = blockIdx.x - prefix_blocks[desc_idx];","+","+    // Decompose local_block into (row_chunk_idx, col_idx) using desc dimensions","     uint32_t chunks_per_block = blockDim.x / skip_domain;","-    uint32_t chunk_in_block = threadIdx.x / skip_domain;","-    uint32_t tid_in_chunk = threadIdx.x % skip_domain;","-    uint32_t row_idx = ctx.local_block_x * chunks_per_block + chunk_in_block;","-    ","-    // Same body as stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel, but reading from desc","-    bool const active_chunk = (row_idx < desc.new_height);","-    // ... (barycentric interpolation using desc.src, desc.trace_height, desc.trace_width)","-    // Output to desc.dst at appropriate offset","+    uint32_t blocks_per_col = (desc.num_x + chunks_per_block - 1) / chunks_per_block;","+    uint32_t col_idx = local_block / blocks_per_col;","+    uint32_t row_block = local_block % blocks_per_col;","+","+    // Same body as existing fold_ple_from_evals_kernel:","+    // - chunk_in_block = threadIdx.x / skip_domain","+    // - tid_in_chunk = threadIdx.x % skip_domain","+    // - row_idx = row_block * chunks_per_block + chunk_in_block","+    // - Barycentric interpolation reads from desc.src at [col_idx * desc.height + row_idx * src_len + ...]","+    // - Writes to desc.dst at [col_idx * desc.num_x + row_idx]"," }"," ```"," ","-The block body is identical to the existing `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` but reads `src`, `dst`, `trace_height`, `new_height` from the descriptor instead of kernel parameters.","+The kernel body is identical to the existing single-trace kernel, but reads `src`, `dst`, `height`, `width`, `num_x` from the descriptor instead of kernel parameters."," ","-### Step 4: Add C launcher function","+### Step 3: Add C launcher"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`"," "," ```c","-extern \"C\" int _batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple(","-    const FoldPleBlockCtx *block_ctx,","+extern \"C\" int _batched_fold_ple_from_evals(","     const FoldPleDesc *descs,","+    const uint32_t *prefix_blocks,","+    uint32_t num_descs,","     uint32_t total_blocks,","     const Fp *omega_skip_pows,","     const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,","-    uint32_t l_skip","+    uint32_t l_skip,","+    bool rotate"," ) {","     uint32_t skip_domain = 1u << l_skip;","     uint32_t block_size = std::max(256u, skip_domain);","-    uint32_t total_warps = block_size / WARP_SIZE;","-    size_t smem_bytes = (skip_domain > WARP_SIZE) ? total_warps * sizeof(FpExt) : 0;","+    size_t smem = (skip_domain > WARP_SIZE) ?","+        (block_size / WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt) : 0;","     ","-    batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel<<<total_blocks, block_size, smem_bytes>>>(","-        block_ctx, descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain","-    );","+    if (rotate) {","+        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<true><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(","+            descs, prefix_blocks, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);","+    } else {","+        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(","+            descs, prefix_blocks, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);","+    }","     return CHECK_KERNEL();"," }"," ```"," ","-### Step 5: Add Rust FFI bindings","+### Step 4: Add Rust FFI bindings"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`"," ","-Add `#[repr(C)]` structs for `FoldPleDesc` and `FoldPleBlockCtx`, plus the extern \"C\" declaration and safe wrapper:","+Add `#[repr(C)]` struct `FoldPleDesc` and the extern \"C\" + safe wrapper for `batched_fold_ple_from_evals`."," ","-```rust","-#[repr(C)]","-pub struct FoldPleDesc {","-    pub src: *const F,","-    pub dst: *mut EF,","-    pub trace_height: u32,","-    pub new_height: u32,","-    pub trace_width: u32,","-}","+### Step 5: Add batched dispatch function"," ","-#[repr(C)]","-pub struct FoldPleBlockCtx {","-    pub desc_idx: u32,","-    pub local_block_x: u32,","-    pub col_idx: u32,","-}","-```","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fold_ple.rs`"," ","-### Step 6: Replace per-trace loop with batched dispatch","+Add:"," ","-**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, in `fold_ple_evals`","+```rust","+pub fn batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate(","+    l_skip: usize,","+    d_omega_skip_pows: &DeviceBuffer<F>,","+    traces: &[(&DeviceMatrix<F>, bool /* need_rot */)],","+    d_inv_lagrange_denoms: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,","+) -> Result<Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>>, FoldPleError>","+```"," ","-Replace lines 714-742 (the per-trace loop) with:","+This function:","+1. Pre-allocates output `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for each trace (matching existing sizes).","+2. Builds two descriptor lists: `descs_plain` (all traces, rotate=false) and `descs_rot` (traces with need_rot, rotate=true).","+3. Computes prefix sums of per-descriptor block counts: `blocks_i = ceil(num_x_i / chunks_per_block) * width_i`.","+4. Uploads descriptors + prefix sums to device.","+5. Launches the batched kernel twice: once for rotate=false, once for rotate=true.","+6. Constructs per-trace `DeviceMatrix<EF>` from the pre-allocated buffers and returns them."," ","-1. **Build descriptors** (CPU): Iterate traces, compute `new_height`, `dst_offset`, create `FoldPleDesc` per trace.","+Skips zero-height/zero-width traces (matching fold_ple.rs:78-80)."," ","-2. **Build BlockCtx array** (CPU): For each descriptor, compute the grid that the per-trace kernel would have used: `grid_x = ceil(new_height / chunks_per_block)`, `grid_y = trace_width`. Create one `FoldPleBlockCtx` per block.","+### Step 6: Wire into fold_ple_evals"," ","-3. **Upload** descriptors and BlockCtx arrays to device (`to_device()`).","+**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, in `fold_ple_evals` (lines 1490-1538)"," ","-4. **Single kernel launch** with `total_blocks = sum of all per-trace block counts`.","+Replace the per-trace `.map()` with:","+1. Collect `(trace_ref, need_rot)` pairs from all traces (preprocessed + cached + common_main).","+2. Call `batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate(...)`.","+3. Redistribute the flat result back into the per-trace `Vec<Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>>>` structure."," ","-5. **Fallback**: If `traces.len() < 10` (e.g., APC 0 with few traces), use the existing per-trace loop to avoid descriptor overhead.","+**Fallback**: If total trace count < 20, use the existing per-trace path."," "," ## Invariants"," ","-1. **Output equivalence**: Each trace's folded output in `folded_evals` must be identical to the per-trace kernel output. The batched kernel uses the exact same computation per block.","+1. **Output equivalence**: Identical computation per block. The descriptor just provides per-trace parameters.","+2. **Destination non-overlap**: Each descriptor's `dst` points to a separately allocated `DeviceBuffer`.","+3. **Shared parameters**: `omega_skip_pows`, `inv_lagrange_denoms`, `l_skip`, `skip_domain` are the same for all traces.","+4. **Block size**: Same as existing: `max(256, skip_domain)`. Shared memory allocation unchanged.","+5. **Per-trace output allocation preserved**: Downstream code (`mat_evals_per_trace`) receives the same per-trace `DeviceMatrix` types.","+6. **save_memory accounting**: `mem_limit` subtraction for common_main (line 1533) uses per-trace buffer sizes — unchanged."," ","-2. **Destination non-overlap**: Each trace writes to a distinct region of `folded_evals` (offset by `dst_offset`). The batched kernel preserves this since each descriptor has its own `dst` pointer.","-","-3. **omega_skip_pows and inv_lagrange_denoms**: Shared across all traces (same for the entire fold_ple_evals call). Passed as kernel parameters, not per-descriptor.","-","-4. **Block size consistency**: The batched kernel uses the same block size as the per-trace kernel (`max(256, skip_domain)`). Shared memory allocation is the same.","-","-5. **APC 0 safety**: The fallback path ensures APC 0 (few traces, below threshold) is unaffected.","-"," ## Measurement Plan"," ","-1. Run benchmarks for APC {0, 100, 300} using `run_pairing.sh`.","-2. Compare Stacked Reduction metric: expect ~8-12ms reduction at APC 300 (75ms → 63-67ms).","-3. Compare STARK excl trace: expect ~8-12ms reduction at APC 300 (1129ms → 1117-1121ms).","-4. Verify APC 0 shows no regression (fallback path active).","-5. nsight: verify `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel` instance count drops from ~797 to ~2-4 (one batched launch per commit group per segment).","+1. Run benchmarks for APC {0, 100, 300}.","+2. Primary metric: Round 0 at APC 300 — expect ~6-8ms reduction (181ms → 173-175ms) from faster fold_ple_evals.","+3. STARK excl trace at APC 300 — expect same ~6-8ms reduction (1129ms → 1121-1123ms).","+4. APC 0: expect no regression (fallback path, < 20 traces per segment).","+5. nsight: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>` instances should drop from ~797 to ~2-4."," "," ## Rollback Criteria"," ","-- Stacked Reduction improvement at APC 300 < 5ms","-- APC 0 regression > 5ms on Stacked Reduction","-- Correctness failure at any APC configuration","+- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 < 3ms","+- APC 0 regression > 5ms on STARK excl trace","+- Correctness failure at any APC config"]}],"originalFile":"# Plan: Batch fold_ple Kernel Launches via Descriptor Array\n\n## Goal\n\nReplace the per-trace sequential loop of `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` GPU kernel launches in `fold_ple_evals` (stacked_reduction.rs:714-742) with a single batched descriptor-array kernel launch. At APC 300 with ~600-800 traces across 2 segments, this eliminates ~790 individual kernel launches and enables concurrent SM utilization across traces.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Rust side: `StackedReductionGpu::fold_ple_evals` (`stacked_reduction.rs:688-788`)\n\nAfter Round 0, this function folds PLE evaluations for each unstacked trace:\n\n```rust\nfor stacked in &self.stacked_per_commit {           // ~2-3 commit groups\n    let folded_evals = DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity(num_x * stacked_width);\n    folded_evals.fill_zero()?;\n    let mut dst_offset = 0;\n    for trace in &stacked.traces {                   // ~300 traces at APC 300\n        stacked_reduction_fold_ple(                  // <-- One kernel launch per trace\n            trace.buffer().as_ptr(), dst, ...,\n            trace.height(), trace.width(), l_skip,\n        )?;\n        dst_offset += new_height * trace.width();\n    }\n    self.q_evals.push(folded_evals);\n}\n```\n\nEach `stacked_reduction_fold_ple` call launches `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` with grid `(ceil(new_height / chunks_per_block), trace_width)` and block `(max(256, skip_domain))`.\n\n### CUDA kernel: `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` (`stacked_reduction.cu:175-229`)\n\nGrid: 2D — `blockIdx.x` selects row chunk, `blockIdx.y` selects column.\nPer-thread: barycentric interpolation of `skip_domain` source values into one output FpExt value.\n\nParameters per trace: `src` (source trace pointer), `dst` (output pointer within folded_evals buffer), `trace_height`, `new_height`, `skip_domain`.\n\n### Why it's slow\n\nnsight profiling shows `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>` (same kernel, different instantiation): **797 instances, 9.5ms total, avg 12μs per instance**.\n\nTwo costs:\n1. **Kernel launch overhead**: ~5μs × 797 = ~4ms. Each launch goes through the CUDA driver.\n2. **Sequential SM utilization**: Each per-trace kernel runs alone on the GPU. Small traces (low width × low height) use few blocks, leaving most of the 128 SMs idle. The next trace's kernel only starts after the previous completes.\n\nWith a batched kernel, all traces' blocks launch simultaneously. The GPU scheduler distributes them across SMs concurrently, converting sum-of-times into max-of-times.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Define descriptor struct\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd a `FoldPleDesc` descriptor:\n\n```c\nstruct FoldPleDesc {\n    const Fp *src;          // source trace pointer\n    FpExt *dst;             // destination within folded_evals buffer\n    uint32_t trace_height;\n    uint32_t new_height;\n    uint32_t trace_width;\n};\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add BlockCtx mapping struct\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd a `FoldPleBlockCtx` that maps each CUDA block to a (descriptor_index, local_block_x, column_idx):\n\n```c\nstruct FoldPleBlockCtx {\n    uint32_t desc_idx;      // index into FoldPleDesc array\n    uint32_t local_block_x; // row chunk index within this trace\n    uint32_t col_idx;       // column index within this trace\n};\n```\n\n### Step 3: Implement batched kernel\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\nAdd `batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel`:\n\n```c\n__global__ void batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel(\n    const FoldPleBlockCtx *block_ctx,\n    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    uint32_t skip_domain\n) {\n    auto ctx = block_ctx[blockIdx.x];\n    auto desc = descs[ctx.desc_idx];\n    \n    uint32_t col_idx = ctx.col_idx;\n    uint32_t chunks_per_block = blockDim.x / skip_domain;\n    uint32_t chunk_in_block = threadIdx.x / skip_domain;\n    uint32_t tid_in_chunk = threadIdx.x % skip_domain;\n    uint32_t row_idx = ctx.local_block_x * chunks_per_block + chunk_in_block;\n    \n    // Same body as stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel, but reading from desc\n    bool const active_chunk = (row_idx < desc.new_height);\n    // ... (barycentric interpolation using desc.src, desc.trace_height, desc.trace_width)\n    // Output to desc.dst at appropriate offset\n}\n```\n\nThe block body is identical to the existing `stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel` but reads `src`, `dst`, `trace_height`, `new_height` from the descriptor instead of kernel parameters.\n\n### Step 4: Add C launcher function\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/stacked_reduction.cu`\n\n```c\nextern \"C\" int _batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple(\n    const FoldPleBlockCtx *block_ctx,\n    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n    uint32_t total_blocks,\n    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    uint32_t l_skip\n) {\n    uint32_t skip_domain = 1u << l_skip;\n    uint32_t block_size = std::max(256u, skip_domain);\n    uint32_t total_warps = block_size / WARP_SIZE;\n    size_t smem_bytes = (skip_domain > WARP_SIZE) ? total_warps * sizeof(FpExt) : 0;\n    \n    batched_stacked_reduction_fold_ple_kernel<<<total_blocks, block_size, smem_bytes>>>(\n        block_ctx, descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain\n    );\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n### Step 5: Add Rust FFI bindings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/stacked_reduction.rs`\n\nAdd `#[repr(C)]` structs for `FoldPleDesc` and `FoldPleBlockCtx`, plus the extern \"C\" declaration and safe wrapper:\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct FoldPleDesc {\n    pub src: *const F,\n    pub dst: *mut EF,\n    pub trace_height: u32,\n    pub new_height: u32,\n    pub trace_width: u32,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct FoldPleBlockCtx {\n    pub desc_idx: u32,\n    pub local_block_x: u32,\n    pub col_idx: u32,\n}\n```\n\n### Step 6: Replace per-trace loop with batched dispatch\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_reduction.rs`, in `fold_ple_evals`\n\nReplace lines 714-742 (the per-trace loop) with:\n\n1. **Build descriptors** (CPU): Iterate traces, compute `new_height`, `dst_offset`, create `FoldPleDesc` per trace.\n\n2. **Build BlockCtx array** (CPU): For each descriptor, compute the grid that the per-trace kernel would have used: `grid_x = ceil(new_height / chunks_per_block)`, `grid_y = trace_width`. Create one `FoldPleBlockCtx` per block.\n\n3. **Upload** descriptors and BlockCtx arrays to device (`to_device()`).\n\n4. **Single kernel launch** with `total_blocks = sum of all per-trace block counts`.\n\n5. **Fallback**: If `traces.len() < 10` (e.g., APC 0 with few traces), use the existing per-trace loop to avoid descriptor overhead.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Output equivalence**: Each trace's folded output in `folded_evals` must be identical to the per-trace kernel output. The batched kernel uses the exact same computation per block.\n\n2. **Destination non-overlap**: Each trace writes to a distinct region of `folded_evals` (offset by `dst_offset`). The batched kernel preserves this since each descriptor has its own `dst` pointer.\n\n3. **omega_skip_pows and inv_lagrange_denoms**: Shared across all traces (same for the entire fold_ple_evals call). Passed as kernel parameters, not per-descriptor.\n\n4. **Block size consistency**: The batched kernel uses the same block size as the per-trace kernel (`max(256, skip_domain)`). Shared memory allocation is the same.\n\n5. **APC 0 safety**: The fallback path ensures APC 0 (few traces, below threshold) is unaffected.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run benchmarks for APC {0, 100, 300} using `run_pairing.sh`.\n2. Compare Stacked Reduction metric: expect ~8-12ms reduction at APC 300 (75ms → 63-67ms).\n3. Compare STARK excl trace: expect ~8-12ms reduction at APC 300 (1129ms → 1117-1121ms).\n4. Verify APC 0 shows no regression (fallback path active).\n5. nsight: verify `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel` instance count drops from ~797 to ~2-4 (one batched launch per commit group per segment).\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Stacked Reduction improvement at APC 300 < 5ms\n- APC 0 regression > 5ms on Stacked Reduction\n- Correctness failure at any APC configuration\n"}}
