{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Bk3d7BtV7aHPe2Ycw7ZwL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch fold_ple_from_evals Kernel Launches via Descriptor Array\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReplace the per-trace sequential `fold_ple_from_evals` GPU kernel launches in `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594) with a single batched descriptor-array kernel. nsight shows `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>`: 797 instances, 9.5ms total at APC 300. The per-trace loop launches one kernel per matrix per trace, serializing on the GPU stream. A batched launch enables concurrent block scheduling across traces.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Entry: `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594)\n10\t\n11\tCalled once per segment at line 619, inside the Round 0 tracing span (after `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, before MLE rounds begin).\n12\t\n13\tThe function iterates all traces and launches `fold_ple_from_evals` per matrix:\n14\t\n15\t```rust\n16\tself.mat_evals_per_trace = ctx.per_trace.iter().map(|(air_idx, air_ctx)| {\n17\t    let mut results: Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>> = Vec::new();\n18\t    // Preprocessed (if exists): fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 kernel launches\n19\t    if let Some(committed) = &air_pk.preprocessed_data {\n20\t        results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n21\t    }\n22\t    // Cached mains: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches each\n23\t    for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains { ... }\n24\t    // Common main: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches\n25\t    results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n26\t    Ok(results)\n27\t}).collect()?;\n28\t```\n29\t\n30\t### `fold_ple_evals_rotate` (fold_ple.rs:16-55)\n31\t\n32\tCalls `fold_ple_evals_gpu` once (rotate=false), and if `need_rot`, once more (rotate=true). Each call allocates a separate output `DeviceBuffer`, then launches the kernel.\n33\t\n34\t### `fold_ple_evals_gpu` → `fold_ple_from_evals` (fold_ple.rs:67-102)\n35\t\n36\tFFI call to `_fold_ple_from_evals` in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`. Kernel: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<ROTATE>`.\n37\t\n38\tGrid: `(ceil(num_x / chunks_per_block), width)`, block: `max(256, skip_domain)`.\n39\t\n40\tPer-thread: barycentric interpolation of `min(height, skip_domain)` source values into one output EF value. When `ROTATE=true`, source values are shifted by one position (modular rotation).\n41\t\n42\t### Parameters per launch\n43\t\n44\t- `src`: matrix data pointer (`*const F`)\n45\t- `dst`: output pointer (`*mut EF`)\n46\t- `omega_skip_pows`: shared across all traces\n47\t- `inv_lagrange_denoms`: shared across all traces\n48\t- `height`, `width`, `l_skip`, `num_x`: per-trace dimensions\n49\t- `rotate`: bool (template parameter)\n50\t\n51\t### Why it's slow at APC 300\n52\t\n53\t797 kernel launches at avg 12μs each = 9.5ms GPU time. Two costs:\n54\t1. **Kernel launch overhead**: ~5μs × 797 = ~4ms of CUDA driver overhead.\n55\t2. **Serial SM utilization**: Small traces (low width × low num_x) produce few blocks, leaving most of the 128 SMs idle while each small kernel runs to completion.\n56\t\n57\tAt APC 0: ~99 AIRs × ~1.3 matrices = ~130 launches across 5 segments, ~26 per segment. Savings proportionally smaller.\n58\t\n59\t## Changes\n60\t\n61\t### Step 1: Define descriptor struct (CUDA side)\n62\t\n63\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n64\t\n65\t```c\n66\tstruct FoldPleDesc {\n67\t    const Fp *src;       // source matrix data pointer\n68\t    FpExt *dst;          // output buffer pointer (non-overlapping per trace)\n69\t    uint32_t height;     // source matrix height\n70\t    uint32_t width;      // source matrix width\n71\t    uint32_t num_x;      // = max(height, skip_domain) / skip_domain\n72\t};\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\t### Step 2: Add batched kernel using prefix-sum block mapping\n76\t\n77\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n78\t\n79\tFollow the existing `batched_nondegen_mle_round_kernel` pattern (in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/mle.cu`): upload a prefix-sum array of cumulative block counts, and each CUDA block binary-searches to find its descriptor index.\n80\t\n81\t```c\n82\ttemplate <bool ROTATE>\n83\t__global__ void batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel(\n84\t    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n85\t    const uint32_t *prefix_blocks,  // prefix_blocks[i] = sum of blocks for descs 0..i-1\n86\t    uint32_t num_descs,\n87\t    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n88\t    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n89\t    uint32_t skip_domain\n90\t) {\n91\t    // Binary search to find which descriptor this block belongs to\n92\t    uint32_t desc_idx = upper_bound(prefix_blocks, num_descs, blockIdx.x) - 1;\n93\t    auto desc = descs[desc_idx];\n94\t    uint32_t local_block = blockIdx.x - prefix_blocks[desc_idx];\n95\t\n96\t    // Decompose local_block into (row_chunk_idx, col_idx) using desc dimensions\n97\t    uint32_t chunks_per_block = blockDim.x / skip_domain;\n98\t    uint32_t blocks_per_col = (desc.num_x + chunks_per_block - 1) / chunks_per_block;\n99\t    uint32_t col_idx = local_block / blocks_per_col;\n100\t    uint32_t row_block = local_block % blocks_per_col;\n101\t\n102\t    // Same body as existing fold_ple_from_evals_kernel:\n103\t    // - chunk_in_block = threadIdx.x / skip_domain\n104\t    // - tid_in_chunk = threadIdx.x % skip_domain\n105\t    // - row_idx = row_block * chunks_per_block + chunk_in_block\n106\t    // - Barycentric interpolation reads from desc.src at [col_idx * desc.height + row_idx * src_len + ...]\n107\t    // - Writes to desc.dst at [col_idx * desc.num_x + row_idx]\n108\t}\n109\t```\n110\t\n111\tThe kernel body is identical to the existing single-trace kernel, but reads `src`, `dst`, `height`, `width`, `num_x` from the descriptor instead of kernel parameters.\n112\t\n113\t### Step 3: Add C launcher\n114\t\n115\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n116\t\n117\t```c\n118\textern \"C\" int _batched_fold_ple_from_evals(\n119\t    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n120\t    const uint32_t *prefix_blocks,\n121\t    uint32_t num_descs,\n122\t    uint32_t total_blocks,\n123\t    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n124\t    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n125\t    uint32_t l_skip,\n126\t    bool rotate\n127\t) {\n128\t    uint32_t skip_domain = 1u << l_skip;\n129\t    uint32_t block_size = std::max(256u, skip_domain);\n130\t    size_t smem = (skip_domain > WARP_SIZE) ?\n131\t        (block_size / WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt) : 0;\n132\t    \n133\t    if (rotate) {\n134\t        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<true><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(\n135\t            descs, prefix_blocks, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);\n136\t    } else {\n137\t        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(\n138\t            descs, prefix_blocks, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);\n139\t    }\n140\t    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n141\t}\n142\t```\n143\t\n144\t### Step 4: Add Rust FFI bindings\n145\t\n146\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n147\t\n148\tAdd `#[repr(C)]` struct `FoldPleDesc` and the extern \"C\" + safe wrapper for `batched_fold_ple_from_evals`.\n149\t\n150\t### Step 5: Add batched dispatch function\n151\t\n152\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fold_ple.rs`\n153\t\n154\tAdd:\n155\t\n156\t```rust\n157\tpub fn batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate(\n158\t    l_skip: usize,\n159\t    d_omega_skip_pows: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n160\t    traces: &[(&DeviceMatrix<F>, bool /* need_rot */)],\n161\t    d_inv_lagrange_denoms: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n162\t) -> Result<Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>>, FoldPleError>\n163\t```\n164\t\n165\tThis function:\n166\t1. Pre-allocates output `DeviceBuffer<EF>` for each trace (matching existing sizes).\n167\t2. Builds two descriptor lists: `descs_plain` (all traces, rotate=false) and `descs_rot` (traces with need_rot, rotate=true).\n168\t3. Computes prefix sums of per-descriptor block counts: `blocks_i = ceil(num_x_i / chunks_per_block) * width_i`.\n169\t4. Uploads descriptors + prefix sums to device.\n170\t5. Launches the batched kernel twice: once for rotate=false, once for rotate=true.\n171\t6. Constructs per-trace `DeviceMatrix<EF>` from the pre-allocated buffers and returns them.\n172\t\n173\tSkips zero-height/zero-width traces (matching fold_ple.rs:78-80).\n174\t\n175\t### Step 6: Wire into fold_ple_evals\n176\t\n177\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, in `fold_ple_evals` (lines 1490-1538)\n178\t\n179\tReplace the per-trace `.map()` with:\n180\t1. Collect `(trace_ref, need_rot)` pairs from all traces (preprocessed + cached + common_main).\n181\t2. Call `batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate(...)`.\n182\t3. Redistribute the flat result back into the per-trace `Vec<Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>>>` structure.\n183\t\n184\t**Fallback**: If total trace count < 20, use the existing per-trace path.\n185\t\n186\t## Invariants\n187\t\n188\t1. **Output equivalence**: Identical computation per block. The descriptor just provides per-trace parameters.\n189\t2. **Destination non-overlap**: Each descriptor's `dst` points to a separately allocated `DeviceBuffer`.\n190\t3. **Shared parameters**: `omega_skip_pows`, `inv_lagrange_denoms`, `l_skip`, `skip_domain` are the same for all traces.\n191\t4. **Block size**: Same as existing: `max(256, skip_domain)`. Shared memory allocation unchanged.\n192\t5. **Per-trace output allocation preserved**: Downstream code (`mat_evals_per_trace`) receives the same per-trace `DeviceMatrix` types.\n193\t6. **save_memory accounting**: `mem_limit` subtraction for common_main (line 1533) uses per-trace buffer sizes — unchanged.\n194\t\n195\t## Measurement Plan\n196\t\n197\t1. Run benchmarks for APC {0, 100, 300}.\n198\t2. Primary metric: Round 0 at APC 300 — expect ~6-8ms reduction (181ms → 173-175ms) from faster fold_ple_evals.\n199\t3. STARK excl trace at APC 300 — expect same ~6-8ms reduction (1129ms → 1121-1123ms).\n200\t4. APC 0: expect no regression (fallback path, < 20 traces per segment).\n201\t5. nsight: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>` instances should drop from ~797 to ~2-4.\n202\t\n203\t## Rollback Criteria\n204\t\n205\t- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 < 3ms\n206\t- APC 0 regression > 5ms on STARK excl trace\n207\t- Correctness failure at any APC config\n208\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FarCk3BdP3QtjwEW43MdxV","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"29129578-02f8-4d10-a31b-4757cc9a1aef","timestamp":"2026-04-16T00:20:24.352Z"}
