{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Er5dW4eKFXuJinTKkuY1Mc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0200-batch-fold-ple-descriptor-array\n2\t\n3\tThe logup_zerocheck `fold_ple_evals` function (mod.rs:1478-1594), called within the Round 0 span, launches one `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel` per matrix per trace in a sequential loop. At APC 300 this creates ~800 individual kernel launches (nsight: 797 instances of `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>`, 9.5ms total, avg 12μs). Each launch serializes on the GPU stream, preventing concurrent SM utilization across traces. Replacing the per-trace loop with a single batched descriptor-array kernel launch enables concurrent processing across all trace matrices, converting serial kernel time into parallel execution while eliminating ~795 kernel launch overhead cycles.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FarCk3BdP3QtjwEW43MdxV","session_id":"97df75af-c1b3-4850-8566-f6b18608e3d5","uuid":"2e92f4a3-8e87-4f84-841a-02b853cff57c","timestamp":"2026-04-16T00:20:25.056Z"}
